From 4bef2a253d97a659f25282a7dffdd2a39a2fb14c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1vivy <1vivy@tutanota.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 15:34:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] infiniti-camera: add the infiniti device camera fragment

Second half of the two-tier camera topology split (task-8 design,
sections 4-5): infiniti-camera.mk inherits the SoC-common camera
fragment (device/oneplus/sm8850-common-camera) plus the
vendor/oplus/camera payload (vendor-tier split deferred per task-8
section 3), and carries the infiniti-bucket device-side camera config:
the family-A odm oemlayer HAL selection (ro.hardware.camera) and the
infiniti vendor-partition '=true' form of ro.camera.disableHeicUltraHDR
(task-8 section 4 rows), both moved out of device/oneplus/sm8850-common
vendor.prop. README replaced with the real repo contract.

Change-Id: I3c363b9709d490c0d23099ee672c492e6d3e089c
---
 README.md          | 61 +++++++++++-----------------------------------
 infiniti-camera.mk | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 45 insertions(+), 47 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 infiniti-camera.mk

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index ea6ab54..984aab0 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1,51 +1,18 @@
-# device_oneplus_infiniti-camera
+# device/oneplus/infiniti-camera
 
-Build-tree path: `device/oneplus/infiniti-camera`
-Branch: `staging/16.0_crdroid` (integration branch for the crDroid 16.0 camera split)
+Per-device camera fragment for infiniti (OnePlus 15, sm8850/kaanapali)
+— the device tier of the two-tier camera topology split (task-8 design).
 
-## Purpose
+Inheritance chain:
 
-Per-device camera tree for the OnePlus 15 "infiniti" (CPH2745, board OP611FL1, prj 24863).
-Carries the camera content that dump evidence proves is device-specific:
+    device/oneplus/infiniti/device.mk
+      -> device/oneplus/infiniti-camera/infiniti-camera.mk
+           -> device/oneplus/sm8850-common-camera/sm8850-common-camera.mk
+           -> vendor/oplus/camera/opluscamera.mk   (payload)
 
-- Family-A vendor camera blob listing: the 180-file `vendor/lib64/camera` drop + vendor hw HAL
-  libs (`camera.qcom.so`, `camera.qcom.sm8850.so`, `camera.qcom.core.so`,
-  `com.qti.chi.{override,offline}.so`) + odm oemlayer (blob bytes stay in `vendor/oplus/camera`).
-- `CameraHWConfiguration.config` (5 logical cameras; infiniti{main,front,ultrawide,tele}).
-- Per-sensor odm tuning (`config/<sensor>`, cfr_bin, dng, 3A libaec/af/pdCustomParam, awb,
-  `com.oplus.node.*`).
-- Per-device configs: `fwk_config.json`, `media_profiles.xml`, `camera_engmode.xml`,
-  `oplus_camera_*`, eis vcfg, facerestore, vainr.
-- Infiniti-only presence files: `com.qti.sensormodule.infiniti*.bin`,
-  `OplusOfflineReprocess.json`, `manifest_mosey.xml`, `p3_to_bt2020_3dlut.bin`,
-  `gamma_masterMode_quick_sdr_conf.json`.
-- Camera/gallery APK package selection (OplusCamera, OppoGallery2, AIUnit, VideoGallery —
-  infiniti builds).
-
-The sm8850-common camera surface (registration vintf/rc, camx impl libs, shared 526-file
-algorithm asset base, system_ext configs) lives in `device_oneplus_sm8850-common-camera`,
-which this tree inherits.
-
-## Evidence basis
-
-Dump analysis (Task 5 of the crDroid sm8850 camera-split plan, 2026-07-03) proved **two vendor
-camera blob provenance families** on sm8850/canoe:
-
-- **Family A = infiniti (+op15)**: 180-file drop; the op15 dump (CPH2747, same board OP611FL1 /
-  prj 24863, older 16.0.5 firmware) differs in only 5/180 files — board-stable.
-- **Family B = macan (CPH2769, 15R) + macanc (PLR110, Ace 6T) + fairlady (PLZ110, 15T)**:
-  201-file drop, 201/201 byte-identical within the trio.
-- Across families only 2/180 files match — families are never mixed; this repo carries the
-  family-A device, and only the ×4-byte-identical surface was commonized.
-
-Source dump for this device: `infiniti_CPH2745_OOS16.0.8_11.A.42` — OxygenOS 16.0.8.300(EX01),
-OTA 11.A.42, fingerprint `OnePlus/CPH2745IN/OP611FL1:16/BP2A.250605.015/...`. Cross-check dump:
-`op15_16.0.5.702` (CPH2747, OxygenOS 16.0.5.703(EX01)). Family-B dumps (macan OTA 11.A.47,
-macanc ColorOS 16.0.8.301 OTA 11.A.62, fairlady ColorOS 16.0.8.300 OTA 11.A.31) are deferred —
-not port targets.
-
-## Content
-
-This repo is scaffolding only for now. The `infiniti-camera.mk` fragment, blob listings,
-sepolicy, and overlays land via Task 12 of the plan, which also adds this project to the build
-manifest. Do not add this repo to a manifest before that content exists.
+Scope: the infiniti-specific camera surface (task-8 section 4
+"infiniti"-bucket rows) — family-A payload selection (odm oemlayer HAL),
+the infiniti vendor-prop forms, and, as the vendor-tier split lands, the
+family-A blob listing (`proprietary-files-camera-infiniti.txt`),
+device-scoped camera sepolicy and camera overlays. Per-sensor tuning
+bytes stay in the vendor payload repo.
diff --git a/infiniti-camera.mk b/infiniti-camera.mk
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f5731ae
--- /dev/null
+++ b/infiniti-camera.mk
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+#
+# Copyright (C) 2026 The LineageOS Project
+#
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+#
+
+# infiniti (OnePlus 15) device camera product fragment (task-8 topology
+# sections 4-5). Inherited from device/oneplus/infiniti/device.mk.
+
+# SoC-common camera surface
+$(call inherit-product, device/oneplus/sm8850-common-camera/sm8850-common-camera.mk)
+
+# OEM camera payload. The vendor-tier common/per-device split is deferred
+# (task-8 section 3): vendor/oplus/camera still hosts both the common
+# registration/asset surface and the infiniti family-A payload
+# (180-file vendor/lib64/camera drop, hw HAL libs, odm oemlayer,
+# per-sensor odm tuning, per-device framework/app camera configs,
+# infiniti-only presence files, camera/gallery APKs — the task-8
+# section 4 "infiniti"-bucket rows).
+$(call inherit-product-if-exists, vendor/oplus/camera/opluscamera.mk)
+
+# infiniti camera properties (moved from device/oneplus/sm8850-common
+# vendor.prop):
+# - ro.hardware.camera selects the family-A odm oemlayer HAL
+#   (task-8 section 4 family-A payload row: "odm oemlayer (v2 + adapter)")
+# - ro.camera.disableHeicUltraHDR uses the infiniti vendor-partition
+#   '=true' form (task-8 section 4 disableHeicUltraHDR row: family-split
+#   prop form, normalize per family)
+PRODUCT_VENDOR_PROPERTIES += \
+    ro.camera.disableHeicUltraHDR=true \
+    ro.hardware.camera=oemlayer.v2
